=== Prompt ===
Who is Darth Vader?

=== Response ===
Darth Vader is a fictional character in the Star Wars franchise, portrayed by British actor David Prowse and voiced by American actor James Earl Jones. He is a primary antagonist in the original trilogy and a main character in the prequel trilogy.

In the Star Wars universe, Anakin Skywalker is a young slave who is discovered by Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi. He is trained as a Jedi and becomes a skilled and powerful warrior. However, he is seduced by the dark side of the Force through manipulation by the Sith Lord, Count Dooku, and the Emperor Palpatine. After a duel with Obi-Wan, during which he is mortally wounded, Anakin is saved by Palpatine but at a terrible cost: his body is saved but horribly disfigured and replaced with mechanical parts, and his soul becomes the Sith Lord Darth Vader.

As Darth Vader, he serves the Emperor and hunts down and eliminates the Jedi. He is the father of Luke Skywalker, who becomes a central figure in the Rebellion against the Galactic Empire. In the original trilogy, Darth Vader plays a major role in the story, with his ultimate redemption and death being a significant part of the saga. In the prequel trilogy, we see Anakin's transformation into Darth Vader and the events that led to his fall to the dark side.

